    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To begin the deployment process for GridFlow CLI, ensure your environment meets standard requirements such as a modern shell environment and sufficient disk space for temporary package manifests. You can install the CLI globally by running the stable curl command which fetches and verifies the latest binary before placing it in your system's executable path. Once the binary is ready, authenticate your session by executing `gridflow auth login`, a step that securely establishes an encrypted handshake between your local machine and our secure vault to validate your corporate identity. Proceed to initialize your local project structure with `gridflow project init`, which generates all necessary manifest files, version locks, and environment-specific configuration templates without altering your existing source code. For the actual release, run `gridflow deploy --env prod` to initiate a full pipeline that handles dependency resolution, builds the container image, and stages it in our production registry. Finally, monitor the output logs carefully for any stage failures, as the CLI will automatically retry failed network requests based on our internal circuit breaker configuration before retrying the final container pull.",
      "source": "target",
